00:06:47,950 --> 00:06:49,470
So now let's take a look at Fluency Builder.

131
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:51,420
Fluency Builder.

132
00:06:52,220 --> 00:07:04,780
So at the beginning of the dialogue, Rebecca is talking to Mr. Parsons about the job and she says, you know, I don't really have that many questions, but when I talked to Miss Childs about the job over the phone, there were some things she wanted to clarify.

133
00:07:05,180 --> 00:07:05,980
So how did she talk to her?

134
00:07:06,060 --> 00:07:07,440
She talked to her over the phone.

135
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:08,180
That's right.

136
00:07:08,380 --> 00:07:18,460
So this is a really good phrase to specify that you received information or you did business talking on the phone, not in person.

137
00:07:18,840 --> 00:07:23,000
OK, so this is a bit strange because we use the preposition over.

138
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,400
You could also say I'm on the phone.

139
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:25,860
That means I'm talking on the phone.

140
00:07:26,800 --> 00:07:29,400
But over the phone means by phone.

141
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:29,600
That's right.

142
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:32,440
Not by mail or email or in person.

143
00:07:32,840 --> 00:07:35,760
But we communicate, we talk over the phone by phone.

144
00:07:36,020 --> 00:07:49,400
So sometimes, for example, people will see a TV commercial with a nice item or device that they want to buy and they will purchase this object, maybe a DVD player over the phone.

145
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:51,520
They will call up this number and order it.

146
00:07:52,360 --> 00:07:58,660
Or you can say, you know, I'm really sorry, Marco, but I don't feel comfortable talking about my banking details over the phone.

147
00:07:59,000 --> 00:07:59,220
That's right.

148
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,920
OK, so that means on the phone.

149
00:08:01,920 --> 00:08:05,860
