153
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:21,400
Don't be nervous.

154
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:23,640
If you have a question, just ask it.

155
00:08:23,890 --> 00:08:24,450
That's right.

156
00:08:25,010 --> 00:08:26,110
So feel free to ask.

157
00:08:26,550 --> 00:08:27,310
Don't worry about it.

158
00:08:27,720 --> 00:08:28,920
Just ask me.

159
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:32,090
It's a very good phrase to give someone or to make someone feel more comfortable.

160
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:33,250
Exactly, exactly.

161
00:08:33,790 --> 00:08:34,030
All right.

162
00:08:34,330 --> 00:08:38,190
And he said that I'll try to fill in the details.

163
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:46,800
OK, so this is an interesting phrase because fill in, you know, on a form, for example, means put your name in a box or fill in some numbers.

164
00:08:46,800 --> 00:08:51,180
But here the details, we think maybe maybe I don't know what the details are.

165
00:08:51,500 --> 00:08:55,100
So to fill them in means to fill in gaps or some blanks.

166
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:56,580
So like, I don't know all the details.

167
00:08:56,760 --> 00:08:59,040
Please tell me the information so that I will know them.

168
00:08:59,220 --> 00:08:59,720
That's right.

169
00:08:59,940 --> 00:09:06,980
So what he's basically saying is I know that you have an idea or a general overview of how things are.

170
00:09:07,410 --> 00:09:11,710
But if you ask me, I can tell you more specific things that fill in the details.

171
00:09:12,030 --> 00:09:15,710
Or, for example, we're going to a party on Saturday night, but I don't know where the party is yet.

172
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:16,510
How about on Friday?

173
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:19,170
I call you to fill you in on the details.

174
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:20,680
Very good.

175
00:09:20,680 --> 00:09:23,680
OK, so those are the phrases that we've prepared for you today.

176
